      {
        "batch": "recipes-gen/trial-1",
        "note": "Two new recipes authored via recipes-gen (tools/seedsmith/seedsmith/adapters/items/recipegen), a small trial batch run end-to-end through plan_run/run_draws/write_corpus and RunLedger (data/seed/items/_runs/recipes-gen.ledger.json) to prove this module's own generation path against real content before committing to a larger run. No live model call was reachable in this environment -- name/flavor were hand-authored as an honest stand-in, the same precedent gemgen used for g2.json (_meta.model 'gemgen/hand-authored-1') and materialgen used for its shard-rungs-1 amendment. recipe.031 (forge) targets an EXISTING, un-recipe'd base type (item.humanoid-head-a-001, head-guard:humanoid:a); recipe.032 (elevate) spends a REAL, currently-issuable shard id (shard.sprout) rather than one of the four legacy shard.* ids the pre-existing 7 broken cost lines in this same corpus use.",
